# ticket-overdue — in-flight spike is In Review and its successor is still a stub:
# the opener's one allowed preface sentence must say the draft is overdue.
NEEDS=chain-inreview
IFS= read -r -d '' PROMPT <<'PROMPT_EOF' || true
Use the spike-board:spike-ticket skill. I want to make a spike ticket.
PROMPT_EOF
IFS= read -r -d '' MUST <<'MUST_EOF' || true
(overdue|still a stub|before .* In Review)
Is this spike the \*\*next step on that path\*\*, or \*\*something new\*\*\?
{{NEXT_KEY}}.*is next
MUST_EOF
IFS= read -r -d '' MUST_NOT <<'MUST_NOT_EOF' || true
[Ll]oading (your|their) board
Isaiah|Austin|Andrew
⟨|⟩
^```
MUST_NOT_EOF
